From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: gs101-pixel: sink 9 V from USB PD chargers

Only a 5 V sink PDO was listed, so a PD charger was always held at
5 V (5 V/2.4 A from a 9/15/20 V brick = ~12 W input), which caps the
battery at ~+1.7 A with the screen off and much less with it on.
Enable the 9 V/2.2 A fixed PDO that was left commented out; this is
what the stock OS asks a non-PPS charger for. tcpci programs the sink
disconnect threshold from the negotiated voltage (auto discharge), and
max77759_charger already sets CHGIN_ILIM from the contract current.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-pixel-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-pixel-common.dtsi
@@ -1148,7 +1148,15 @@
 						| PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM
 						| PDO_FIXED_HIGHER_CAP
 						| PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE))
-				     /* PDO_FIXED(9000, 2200, 0) */
+				     /*
+				      * Local (Nura): 9 V like the stock OS on a
+				      * non-PPS charger. The max77759 buck takes
+				      * it directly; the charger driver follows
+				      * the contract's current as its input limit
+				      * and fast-charge current stays at its own
+				      * limit. PPS needs the direct charger.
+				      */
+				     PDO_FIXED(9000, 2200, 0)
 				     /* PDO_PPS_APDO(5000, 11000, 3000) */>;
 			sink-vdos = <VDO_IDH(1, 1, IDH_PTYPE_PERIPH, 0,
 					     IDH_PTYPE_DFP_HOST, 2, 0x18d1)
